WEBVTT

00:05.604 --> 00:08.534
Why did you make that wish
on the wishing stones?

00:11.374 --> 00:14.704
Why did you want to become an adult?

00:20.654 --> 00:23.514
It's because... because I'm a burden.

00:24.154 --> 00:30.454
I'm just a burden to you, Hiro!
I always have been.

00:34.564 --> 00:38.194
But I'm not an adult at all!

00:40.274 --> 00:45.704
Even though I've gotten this big,
I'm nothing but a nuisance to you!

00:47.174 --> 00:49.164
I'm sorry.

00:53.854 --> 00:55.114
Karada.

01:02.594 --> 01:04.364
Let's go together!

01:04.364 --> 01:07.294
Let's go home together, Miss Shoko!

01:11.664 --> 01:12.934
Let's go back together.

01:15.374 --> 01:16.304
Okay!

01:19.304 --> 01:23.044
Something reached for but cannot be grasped...

01:24.114 --> 01:28.054
Something that strays from that hand,
going far away...

01:29.314 --> 01:33.654
People will always pursue such things.

01:34.654 --> 01:38.024
And before long, become lost.

01:44.104 --> 01:48.564
This is our story of one such summer.

02:06.854 --> 02:08.324
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

02:08.324 --> 02:11.994
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow
The children's graffiti

02:11.994 --> 02:12.424
Living for the Day
After Tomorrow

02:12.764 --> 02:16.424
That has blossomed on the asphalt

02:17.204 --> 02:20.824
Shimmers in the waves of heat

02:21.674 --> 02:24.504
And has begun to walk

02:24.644 --> 02:29.474
At that promised hill

02:29.474 --> 02:33.104
That no one knows

02:33.654 --> 02:38.354
Encounter the miraculous time called "today"

02:38.354 --> 02:43.124
That comes only once - feel it

02:43.124 --> 02:47.294
Chase the flowing clouds

02:47.294 --> 02:51.634
Even now, they seem in your grasp

02:51.634 --> 02:56.004
A premonition, heart beating with excitement

02:56.004 --> 03:00.634
A destiny that has begun to move

03:00.744 --> 03:05.114
So bright that you awaken

03:05.114 --> 03:09.144
Hotter even than the morning sun

03:09.384 --> 03:13.284
Sparkling without end

03:13.624 --> 03:20.924
Embraced in the season of light

03:28.204 --> 03:30.174
IOKAWA Hiro
Karada

03:35.514 --> 03:36.304
Yes!

03:51.424 --> 03:53.054
Good morning!

03:54.994 --> 03:56.654
Good morning...

04:13.784 --> 04:15.874
Hey. A little help?

04:24.064 --> 04:25.224
There we go.

04:30.064 --> 04:32.464
What are you doing, Karada?

04:33.204 --> 04:36.404
I could have reached it
without getting on the chair.

04:38.744 --> 04:40.804
But out of habit, I'd already...

04:44.744 --> 04:48.744
A Place to Return To

04:49.414 --> 04:51.484
Okay, I'm going now.

04:51.484 --> 04:52.854
See you when you get back!

05:10.904 --> 05:13.004
Say, Miss Shoko?

05:14.374 --> 05:15.344
What is it?

05:18.414 --> 05:23.544
I'm glad that you'll be staying with us for a while.

05:24.024 --> 05:26.854
Well, until I get settled into things, I guess.

05:34.834 --> 05:36.324
Oh, it's all right!

05:58.354 --> 06:00.254
Hey, Karada?

06:00.554 --> 06:02.784
Yes? What is it?

06:05.664 --> 06:07.634
He was very kind.

06:08.234 --> 06:12.664
My mother and father talked about Hiro often,

06:12.664 --> 06:16.794
so when I met him, somehow
it didn't seem like the first time.

06:17.074 --> 06:18.594
Really...

06:21.814 --> 06:26.444
She's been raised this whole time
as Karada lokawa.

06:27.514 --> 06:31.244
She doesn't know we're not blood-related.

06:34.754 --> 06:37.094
A History of Kanocho

06:37.094 --> 06:38.964
Kanocho Anecdotes

06:38.964 --> 06:41.654
LOCAL
HISTORY

06:48.274 --> 06:49.864
Knowing nothing of the truth...

06:51.374 --> 06:54.434
Simply wanting to become an adult
for her brother's sake...

06:55.514 --> 07:00.474
Kanocho
Public Library

07:07.524 --> 07:11.184
Am I all right with not going back to normal?

07:11.394 --> 07:14.454
Can we even go back?

07:15.794 --> 07:19.464
My-mother-said-to-pick-this-ONE!

07:21.734 --> 07:25.174
My-mother-said-to-pick-this-ONE!

07:25.974 --> 07:27.944
Ah! You moved!

07:29.414 --> 07:31.204
Come on, Shoko!

07:33.244 --> 07:35.214
Let's play together!

07:36.014 --> 07:39.384
Forget about Nogami. She won't play.

07:39.824 --> 07:41.894
Huh? But...

07:41.894 --> 07:44.794
She doesn't wanna play with us.

07:45.394 --> 07:46.824
C'mon, let's go.

07:47.494 --> 07:50.764
Hands have always been extended toward me.

07:51.604 --> 07:53.934
And to those hands, I've...

07:58.574 --> 08:01.004
My-mother-said-to-pick-this-ONE!

08:03.614 --> 08:05.084
What's the matter?

08:07.454 --> 08:11.524
You're looking sort of down in the dumps.
You get in a fight with your friends?

08:11.524 --> 08:13.684
Uh, no...

08:14.394 --> 08:16.914
So why aren't you playing with them?

08:18.094 --> 08:22.084
I-I only just moved here.

08:22.464 --> 08:25.624
Oh, is that so? Me, too.

08:26.204 --> 08:28.724
I moved here just the other day.

08:28.974 --> 08:31.874
Still, this was where I was born. Kanocho.

08:33.204 --> 08:37.844
Work kept my parents moving us
all over the place...

08:37.844 --> 08:39.834
But we ended up coming back here.

08:40.184 --> 08:43.924
It had been so long that I was
wondering what it would be like,

08:43.924 --> 08:47.374
but this town hasn't changed one bit!

08:52.224 --> 08:56.394
Hey, you there! Let this girl here play with you!

08:56.994 --> 08:59.024
She said she's just moved here!

08:59.334 --> 09:00.594
Okay, sure!

09:01.174 --> 09:03.374
N-no, I'm fine! Really!

09:03.374 --> 09:06.864
But why? It's best to make friends
as soon as you can, right?

09:09.244 --> 09:11.384
Come on, don't be bashful!

09:11.384 --> 09:15.614
Go on, go out there! C'mon, hurry, get up, hurry!

09:15.614 --> 09:17.744
I said I was fine, didn't I?!

09:21.694 --> 09:26.694
I-I'm sorry. But in any case, I'll pass.

09:26.694 --> 09:28.394
If you'll excuse me.

09:30.064 --> 09:32.534
What's with you? That's not very social!

09:33.334 --> 09:34.804
What's her problem?

09:34.934 --> 09:38.334
She's old enough that she should
be able to play with other kids...

09:41.274 --> 09:43.174
COFFEE SHOP
RABURUN

09:43.174 --> 09:44.084
COFFEE SHOP
RABURUN
Huh? You found Karada?

09:44.084 --> 09:45.804
Huh? You found Karada?

09:46.284 --> 09:50.054
So she's all right then! I'm so glad!

09:50.054 --> 09:55.044
She went by herself to stay at a
relative's house. She called yesterday.

09:55.554 --> 09:57.524
When is she coming back?

09:57.894 --> 10:00.724
Uh... Well...

10:01.734 --> 10:04.024
She'll be there the whole summer vacation.

10:04.334 --> 10:07.424
But why didn't she say anything first?

10:07.874 --> 10:09.834
That's not like her.

10:11.844 --> 10:15.774
Well, maybe it's a rebellious phase.

10:19.614 --> 10:23.554
A-anyway, sorry to have gotten you so worried.

10:23.814 --> 10:27.844
But everything's all right now. So tell Tetsu that...

10:28.394 --> 10:29.494
He hasn't shown up yet, has he?

10:29.494 --> 10:30.864
Tetsu?

10:30.864 --> 10:33.694
Tetsu is, uh...

10:36.594 --> 10:38.594
Going somewhere?

10:39.504 --> 10:43.634
Were you intending to deceive me again?
Well, Tetsumasa?

10:43.874 --> 10:47.274
Y-you've got it wrong! I was just, uh...

10:47.274 --> 10:48.544
Unbelievable!

10:48.544 --> 10:52.674
This is like the summer festival...
If you want to leave, just say so!

10:53.014 --> 10:56.414
I don't recall raising the sort of child

10:56.414 --> 11:00.024
who'd neglect the things he should do
to do only what he WANTS to do!

11:00.024 --> 11:04.724
Yet time and again, what with your father
being so busy with work, it's up to me to...

11:07.224 --> 11:08.694
Thank you for the food!

11:09.534 --> 11:12.364
Sorry it was just a simple vegetable stir fry...

11:12.604 --> 11:14.004
It was delicious!

11:14.004 --> 11:16.764
It's been a while since I'd had your cooking.

11:17.234 --> 11:19.734
Almost a week, wouldn't you say?

11:21.514 --> 11:23.134
Thanks for the food.

11:25.884 --> 11:28.044
Oh, let me!

11:33.184 --> 11:34.484
It's one of our rules.

11:38.724 --> 11:41.924
Whoever doesn't cook
has to clean.

11:43.394 --> 11:46.234
Well, I'm going to draw the bath water.

11:46.234 --> 11:47.534
Thank you.

12:28.644 --> 12:30.074
Ah, thanks.

12:42.654 --> 12:45.294
Miss Shoko! That's all right, I'll-

12:45.294 --> 12:45.564
Karada.
Miss Shoko! That's all right, I'll-

12:45.564 --> 12:46.424
Karada.

12:58.044 --> 12:59.594
Well, I'm going now.

13:00.074 --> 13:01.334
See you when you get back!

13:04.114 --> 13:05.704
Hiro!

13:14.754 --> 13:16.124
It's a string.

13:18.824 --> 13:20.164
Sorry...

13:20.164 --> 13:22.524
I-I'm sorry.

13:24.764 --> 13:25.964
Okay, bye.

13:30.104 --> 13:31.094
Nogami.

13:35.674 --> 13:36.804
What is it?

13:40.314 --> 13:41.574
Well...

13:42.484 --> 13:45.824
I searched the books on local history
at the library yesterday.

13:45.824 --> 13:49.014
But there was nothing at all
about the wishing stones.

13:49.554 --> 13:51.084
I know.

13:51.964 --> 13:55.954
I went by there too. On the way back from work.

13:59.504 --> 14:01.364
I'm happy that you're here, Shoko.

14:02.774 --> 14:05.794
To be honest, I still don't really understand...

14:06.774 --> 14:09.804
How I should, uh, interact with her.

14:11.444 --> 14:14.074
I should know it in my head, but...

14:14.514 --> 14:18.714
It's only because you're around
that I've got sort of an idea.

14:20.424 --> 14:23.784
Would you mind staying with us a while longer?

14:24.294 --> 14:27.824
You haven't changed.
Always thinking of yourself.

14:30.264 --> 14:31.494
I'm sorry.

14:31.904 --> 14:34.364
Karada told me the same thing yesterday.

14:34.834 --> 14:36.774
That she's glad I'm here.

14:38.144 --> 14:39.734
It was wrong of me.

14:44.144 --> 14:46.844
Don't worry, I'll stick around for you guys.

14:47.854 --> 14:50.684
Because I can't find a way to go back to normal.

14:51.784 --> 14:53.524
Is that all you had to say?

14:53.524 --> 14:54.494
Yes.

14:54.494 --> 14:56.324
Then I'll be going.

14:57.154 --> 14:59.024
You haven't changed either.

15:00.294 --> 15:03.454
You're mad, aren't you?
Just open up and be angry!

15:04.204 --> 15:06.294
Someone told me something
like that yesterday, too.

15:20.744 --> 15:23.274
What's not "social" about me?

15:24.884 --> 15:27.214
What's the right way to "open up"?!

15:30.864 --> 15:33.594
My, Kotomi, how you've changed!

15:33.764 --> 15:36.164
You've become the picture of a young lady!

15:36.164 --> 15:39.834
How nice to see you again.
How long has it been, I wonder.

15:39.834 --> 15:41.374
Four years!

15:41.374 --> 15:43.864
But inside, I haven't changed at all!

15:44.304 --> 15:46.744
Anyway, Tetsu sure has gotten bigger!

15:47.244 --> 15:51.384
This boy, honestly. He was so depressed
when you moved away.

15:51.384 --> 15:55.114
There's quite an age difference
between him and his sister, yes?

15:55.114 --> 15:59.024
But as you are just two years older,
he looked to you like an older sister.

15:59.024 --> 16:01.894
All I did was drag him around the place with me.

16:01.894 --> 16:04.984
Sorry for bringing him back after curfew
so many times...

16:05.324 --> 16:10.364
Say, Kotomi, would you mind
looking after Tetsumasa's studies?

16:10.364 --> 16:16.204
He's been so busy recently that he still has
half of his summer homework left.

16:16.334 --> 16:20.974
But I never once did a good job of my own
summer homework, you know!

16:20.974 --> 16:24.134
Studies, huh? I wonder if I'll even understand it.

16:28.314 --> 16:32.374
Wow, what a handful! Your mom's
the same as always, huh?

16:32.724 --> 16:34.994
That was a nice showdown
between you two just now.

16:34.994 --> 16:38.764
You haven't changed either, uh...

16:38.764 --> 16:40.194
Miss Shiozaki.

16:40.194 --> 16:43.634
Just call me Kotomi! Like you used to.

16:44.034 --> 16:46.464
Anyway, what are you doing?

16:49.534 --> 16:51.304
Come on, give me a break!
You actually planned on studying?!

16:51.304 --> 16:53.544
Math Drills
Come on, give me a break!
You actually planned on studying?!

16:53.544 --> 16:54.094
Come on, give me a break!
You actually planned on studying?!

16:57.114 --> 16:59.744
More to the point, Tetsu...

17:01.384 --> 17:04.354
You've gotten way too big!
That's against the rules!

17:06.584 --> 17:09.314
I-It's not like I wanted to get like this!

17:09.854 --> 17:13.294
What? Are you blushing? How cute!

17:13.724 --> 17:15.594
Hey, you wanna go have fun somewhere?

17:15.864 --> 17:18.384
But...

17:18.704 --> 17:22.294
It'll be fine! We can just sneak out the window.

17:23.904 --> 17:26.564
If I do that again, my mom will kill me.

17:27.204 --> 17:30.074
So you've done it before!

17:32.044 --> 17:33.384
Just recently.

17:33.384 --> 17:35.004
I'm impressed!

17:36.284 --> 17:40.724
Parents worry about their kids' futures
and go on about this and that,

17:40.724 --> 17:45.424
but I think the most important thing
is the present, what YOU want to do.

17:47.834 --> 17:51.354
Still, parents can go off if you DON'T have
something you want to do, too.

17:52.304 --> 17:54.704
Your house must've been nice.

17:54.704 --> 17:56.634
You always seemed, like, super free.

17:57.534 --> 18:01.064
Well, there's always the story of
how they simply gave up on me...

18:03.944 --> 18:06.014
They seem like they regret it now,

18:06.014 --> 18:10.784
like things wouldn't have turned out this way
if they'd tried a little harder to raise me properly.

18:11.884 --> 18:16.094
But anyway, instead of thinking
about the past or the future,

18:16.094 --> 18:18.354
I just want to have fun in the present.

18:22.694 --> 18:23.794
Wait up!

18:23.794 --> 18:24.604
Look out!

18:24.604 --> 18:26.094
Come on, wait!

18:44.354 --> 18:46.114
Let's play together!

18:50.094 --> 18:52.424
I-I'm fine.

18:52.764 --> 18:54.354
Let's play together!

18:57.964 --> 19:00.764
Forget about her. She won't play.

19:01.474 --> 19:03.034
Huh? But...

19:03.034 --> 19:05.374
She doesn't wanna play with us.

19:05.704 --> 19:06.864
C'mon, let's go.

19:10.874 --> 19:11.934
Got your shadow!

19:19.184 --> 19:21.584
You're It! You're It!

19:23.494 --> 19:24.794
Oh my gosh!

19:24.794 --> 19:26.424
Eew, what is this?!

19:26.424 --> 19:28.554
What's something like this doing here?!

19:33.564 --> 19:34.904
Got your shadow.

19:35.774 --> 19:37.104
That's a kid for you.

19:38.744 --> 19:40.074
Now you're asking for it!

20:02.634 --> 20:04.394
Bye-Bye!
See you!

20:13.704 --> 20:15.074
Miss Shoko!

20:18.384 --> 20:20.474
Where were you?

20:26.224 --> 20:27.884
I was so worried!

20:32.794 --> 20:34.384
Come on, let's go home.

20:58.324 --> 21:01.154
Who are those two?

21:04.764 --> 21:06.854
Yes, hello?

21:07.934 --> 21:09.954
Aah. Yes.

21:11.734 --> 21:13.904
What? Tetsu?

21:13.904 --> 21:16.504
Yeah. Uh-huh.

21:16.504 --> 21:18.204
I have no idea.

21:18.844 --> 21:20.604
You're worrying too much.

21:20.604 --> 21:23.374
He'll get hungry and come home before long.

21:26.714 --> 21:29.184
Hey! You there, Runaway Boy!

21:29.884 --> 21:31.254
Let me stay here for a while.

21:31.254 --> 21:33.554
Mom is in a frenzy, you know.

21:33.554 --> 21:35.424
I'm living for the moment!

21:35.424 --> 21:36.584
Huh?

21:37.424 --> 21:39.764
I said, I'm living for the moment!

21:39.764 --> 21:40.984
Yeah, yeah.

21:41.634 --> 21:45.694
I'm serious! I have to search for lokawa!

21:46.134 --> 21:47.654
They've already found her.

21:49.034 --> 21:50.124
Karada.

21:52.144 --> 21:57.404
But... Well, there's no use standing
around talking. Let's go inside.

21:59.114 --> 22:01.774
H-hey! What's going on?

22:04.354 --> 22:07.254
Sis! SIS!!

22:14.664 --> 22:20.904
Wearing unfamiliar shoes

22:20.904 --> 22:25.634
Each step a pain that I endure

22:27.074 --> 22:33.344
And yet I walk

22:33.344 --> 22:38.144
Because I have a place to return to

22:38.924 --> 22:47.064
I stare at myself

22:47.064 --> 22:51.654
And notice something I'd lost

22:54.804 --> 23:00.974
I want to be with you

23:00.974 --> 23:07.684
To feel it, near and far

23:07.684 --> 23:13.554
To keep creating each normal day

23:13.554 --> 23:20.194
With you, my beloved

23:20.194 --> 23:27.624
To say "I'm home,"
remove my shoes and hold you

23:27.864 --> 23:32.704
My sweet home

23:46.054 --> 23:52.224
Amino is my friend. He's very tall
and a little clumsy.

23:52.924 --> 23:57.424
Everyone in class is afraid of him,
but I like him very much!

23:58.104 --> 24:04.304
Still, I can't meet him right now.
Because the person I am now isn't me.

24:05.744 --> 24:07.574
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:07.574 --> 24:08.414
Next episode
Summer's Eternity
Next time, on Living for the Day After Tomorrow:

24:08.414 --> 24:10.074
Next episode
Summer's Eternity
"Summer's Eternity"

